rndis_host: allow larger RX URBs so the modem can batch frames

The stock driver sets rx_urb_size to ~one MTU and advertises that as the
RNDIS max_transfer_size, so the peripheral sends one ethernet frame per USB
transfer. rndis_rx_fixup() already demuxes multiple frames per transfer, so a
larger RX URB lets the modem batch, cutting per-completion CPU on the RX core
(the ~300 Mbps single-core softirq bottleneck on the FM350-GL / Cortex-A9).

New module param rndis_rx_urb_mult (default 1 = stock). Set >1 and re-bind the
interface to enlarge the RX URB (e.g. 8 -> ~16 KB). Built-in driver, so the
param lives at /sys/module/rndis_host/parameters/rndis_rx_urb_mult.

--- a/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c
--- a/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c
@@ -284,6 +284,15 @@
 	.ndo_validate_addr	= eth_validate_addr,
 };
 
+/* Enlarge the RNDIS RX URB so the peripheral may batch several ethernet
+ * frames per USB transfer (rndis_rx_fixup() already demuxes them). Stock size
+ * caps max_transfer_size at ~1 packet, the RX throughput bottleneck on weak
+ * CPUs. Multiplier is a module param (1 = stock). */
+static unsigned int rndis_rx_urb_mult = 1;
+module_param(rndis_rx_urb_mult, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rndis_rx_urb_mult,
+	"Multiply RNDIS RX URB size to allow device RX batching (1=stock; set 8 for ~16KB to allow batching)");
+
 int
 generic_rndis_bind(struct usbnet *dev, struct usb_interface *intf, int flags)
 {
@@ -343,6 +352,8 @@
 
 	dev->rx_urb_size = dev->hard_mtu + (dev->maxpacket + 1);
 	dev->rx_urb_size &= ~(dev->maxpacket - 1);
+	if (rndis_rx_urb_mult > 1)
+		dev->rx_urb_size *= rndis_rx_urb_mult;
 	u.init->max_transfer_size = cpu_to_le32(dev->rx_urb_size);
 
 	net->netdev_ops = &rndis_netdev_ops;
